From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 06n-arch <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:55:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 33/57] panvk: Only enable cull distance when the VS lowering
 found the output (06n-arch)

pan_nir_lower_cull_distance_vs only matches store_deref, but the
multiview path runs nir_split_var_copies, which leaves the cull array
written through copy_deref. The pass then adds no
VARYING_SLOT_CULL_PRIMITIVE output while cull_distance_array_size still
enables the fragment prolog, which looks that slot up in the VS varying
layout: an assert in debug builds, a NULL dereference in release.

Lower var copies before the pass, and only report a cull distance size
to the compiler (and so to the prolog key) when the pass made progress.

Local fixup on top of mesa!43156, ported to the current mesa!40343.
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
index b4931fb1eef..f0a9afa063b 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
@@ -1623,7 +1623,15 @@ panvk_compile_shader(struct panvk_device *dev,
                var->data.location - VERT_ATTRIB_GENERIC0;
          }
 
-         NIR_PASS(_, nir, pan_nir_lower_cull_distance_vs);
+         /* The cull lowering only matches store_deref, so lower the
+          * copy_derefs the multiview path leaves behind. If it still finds
+          * nothing, leave cull off: the prolog would look for a
+          * VARYING_SLOT_CULL_PRIMITIVE output the VS doesn't have. */
+         bool lowered_cull = false;
+         if (nir->info.cull_distance_array_size > 0) {
+            NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_var_copies);
+            NIR_PASS(lowered_cull, nir, pan_nir_lower_cull_distance_vs);
+         }
 
          nir_assign_io_var_locations(nir, nir_var_shader_out);
          panvk_lower_nir_io(nir);
@@ -1639,7 +1647,8 @@ panvk_compile_shader(struct panvk_device *dev,
          }
 
          inputs.clip_distance_array_size = nir->info.clip_distance_array_size;
-         inputs.cull_distance_array_size = nir->info.cull_distance_array_size;
+         inputs.cull_distance_array_size =
+            lowered_cull ? nir->info.cull_distance_array_size : 0;
 
          if (v == PANVK_VS_VARIANT_SW)
             panvk_nir_lower_compute_vs(nir, inputs.gpu_id);
